{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5613) in the go-unix-utils code generation pipeline. The task requires extending `cmd/vdir/main.go` to implement four SRD requirements from srd108-vdir:\n   - **R1.5**: Default to current directory (\".\") when no arguments given\n   - **R1.6**: Accept all flags that ls accepts (vdir is identical to ls except default format and quoting)\n   - **R2.1**: Exit 0 when all listed paths accessed and output written successfully\n   - **R2.2**: Exit 1 on minor problems (permission denied, file not found), print diagnostic to stderr, continue processing\n   \n   Design constraints: Extend existing code without rewriting R1.1-R1.4 functionality, preserve SIGPIPE handler.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU vdir is equivalent to `ls -l -b` (long format with C-style escaping)\n   - Differential testing against `gvdir` (Homebrew GNU coreutils reference binary)\n   - `pkg/sys` for SIGPIPE handling and file metadata\n   - `pkg/format` for column alignment and human-readable sizes\n   - Exit code contract: 0=success, 1=minor error (file not found), 2=serious error (invalid option)\n   - C-style backslash escaping for non-printable characters\n   - The execution constitution mandates: no git commands, E8 (40-line function limit), E3 (no scope creep), write all files before building\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd108-vdir.yaml**\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1.1-R1.6, R2.1-R2.4\n     - R1.5: \"When no directory arguments are given, must default to the current directory ('.').\"\n     - R1.6: \"Must accept all flags that ls accepts. vdir is identical to ls except for the default format (-l) and default quoting style (-b). All other behavior is inherited from ls.\"\n     - R2.1: \"Must exit 0 when all listed paths are accessed and output is written successfully.\"\n     - R2.2: \"Must exit 1 when a minor problem occurs (permission denied, file not found). Must print a diagnostic to stderr and continue processing remaining entries.\"\n     - non_goals: no color by default, no multi-column default, no recursive by default\n\n   - **cmd/vdir/main.go** (existing, 495 lines)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R1.4, R2.3, R2.4\n     - Has `options` struct, `fileEntry` struct, `longRow` struct\n     - `main()` calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, `parseArgs()`, and `os.Exit(run(...))`\n     - `parseArgs()` handles short flags, `--help`, `--version`, `--color`, `--` separator\n     - `parseShortFlags()` handles: 1, l, g, n, C, x, a, A, d, f, F, h, i, R, r, s, t, S, U, v, and silently accepts: b, B, c, G, H, k, L, m, N, o, p, q, Q, u, X, Z\n     - `run()` already defaults to `paths = []string{\".\"}` when no paths given (R1.5 already done)\n     - **BUG**: `classifyPaths()` line 209 sets `exitCode = 2` on `sys.Lstat` failure, but R2.2 requires exit code 1 for file-not-found/permission-denied\n     - `listDir()`, `sortEntries()`, `writeOutput()`, `writeLong()`, `buildRow()`, `formatMode()`, `formatTime()`, `lookupName()`, `escapeC()`, `sysErrMsg()`, `capitalize()`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation hasn't started\n   - Key bug identified: In `classifyPaths()` at line 209, `exitCode = 2` should be `exitCode = 1` per R2.2\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R1.5 (default to \".\") is already implemented in the `run()` function\n   - Identified that R2.1 (exit 0 on success) is already implemented via the `exitCode` variable starting at 0\n   - Identified that R2.2 has a bug: `classifyPaths()` sets exit code 2 instead of 1 for access errors\n   - R1.6 (accept all ls flags) needs analysis of whether all GNU ls flags are covered in the current parser\n\n6. All